<main>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <article class="hero-card panel" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Master plan</p>
      <h1>This website is the front door, not the whole platform.</h1>
      <p>PAPR still needs the deeper operational systems behind the public site: inventory-backed raffle logic, draw scheduling, winner publication, admin review tools, compliance handling, and monitoring.</p>
    </article>
    <aside class="hero-aside panel" data-reveal>
      <p class="kicker">Recommended build order</p>
      <h2>Trust language first, engine integrity second, polish after.</h2>
      <p>The public experience should look serious, but it also has to be backed by a real raffle engine and audit trail.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel" data-reveal>
    <div class="timeline-grid">
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <span>1</span>
        <h3>Brand, trust language, and sitemap</h3>
        <p>Set the public tone, page structure, and disclosures before the deeper systems surface publicly.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <span>2</span>
        <h3>Raffle engine and audit model</h3>
        <p>Inventory ledger, hold expiry, sellout locking, state transitions, and draw event logging come next.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <span>3</span>
        <h3>Checkout and account foundations</h3>
        <p>Secure payment, order confirmation, ticket history, and notification flows give the platform its backbone.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <span>4</span>
        <h3>Admin and scheduling tools</h3>
        <p>Operations need raffle creation, draw assignment, content editing, and audit review before launch.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <span>5</span>
        <h3>Winner publishing and support</h3>
        <p>Archive pages, support pathways, and rules links make public trust durable after the first launch.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <span>6</span>
        <h3>Phase-two polish</h3>
        <p>Broadcast tooling, richer CMS flows, advanced analytics, and deeper proof packages can follow the safe launch shape.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
